      "notes": [
        "The elementary functions are generic over the float type and call Rust's `f32` methods for `Float32` (single-precision libm), so `sqrt(-1)`, `asin(2)`, `(-1) ** 0.5` and `log(-1)` are NaN and `sin(±inf)` is NaN in `Float32` as in `Float64`. `log(0)` is `ln(0) / ln(base)`, -inf for any base above 1.",
        "Read at tag py-2.1.0 (commit 7f902bd3). The streaming engine evaluates expressions through polars-expr on each morsel (crates/polars-stream/src/expression.rs), so these kernels serve both engines."
